# UIR-22 integration — serial engine evidence

Runner: `docs/implementation/ui-recreation/tickets/UIR-22-full-integration.md`.
Engine: Godot 4.7.2 (`/Applications/Godot.app/Contents/MacOS/Godot`), macOS.
Serial discipline: one engine at a time, `pgrep -x Godot` guard before every launch
(`/tmp/padel-uir22/run-audits.sh` refuses to start while another instance is up).
A red engine line is counted as a failure even when the audit exits 0; the per-audit
`engine_errors` column below is that count.

## 1. What the playable path now is

`--ui=new` is the default (`main_menu.gd::_ready`): a `--ui=legacy` run keeps the
ported column, a harness can also set `ui_legacy = true` before the tree. The playable
host registers **all twelve recreated Control screens** on `ScreenRouter` under the
router's own ids and drives them through UIR-05's bridge; `game` stays without a
Control scene by design (the match is `Match.tscn`, launched through
`Config.pending_mode`). `Main.tscn` mounts the **result screen** when
`Config.pending_result` is set (consumed once), so the loop is
menu → modes → characters → arena → match → result → rematch/menu.

Seams landed (handles):

| seam | where |
| --- | --- |
| result handoff | `match_config.gd::pending_result` / `take_pending_result()`; `match_controller.gd::result_payload()`, `finish_route(dry_run)` |
| pause state | `match_controller.gd::set_match_paused(bool)` (explicit, idempotent), overlay echo `PauseOverlay.set_match_paused`; ESC walks the card's own steps; rematch/`start_match` clear the pause |
| overlay/tutorial/touch mount | `match_controller.gd` layer build, gated on `engine_driven` so headless lanes stay light |
| menu host | `main_menu.gd::_mount_ui_prototype` (bridge per screen change, OSK panel bound to the lane's own model, `range_changed` handed to the screen, stored language applied at boot) |
| OSK | `OskPanel.bind_model` + `set_osk_targets` only while the model is open; dismissed → targets withdrawn |
| ranges | `SettingsScreen` focus rows now carry the row's own min/max/step/value (the wave-3 carried-keys seam was unused before); `PauseOverlay.set_row_value` applies a model-stepped value through the row's own handler |
| locale | `hud.gd` no longer forces Italian (`HUD_LANG` gone): one locale drives menu and match |
| stage | `project.godot [display]` 1280x720, `canvas_items` + `keep` |

## 2. End-to-end, with real data (uir22_integration_audit)

`uir22_integration_audit.gd` — **PASS 71/71, 0 engine errors**, exit 0. Highlights, all
against real state:

- twelve screens registered, one mounted at a time; every id mounts and unmounts;
- a real confirm on `menu/PlayButton` dispatches through the bridge and lands on `modes`;
- a quick match, played out with `ScriptedPlayer` (18 144 ticks), produces
  `{"winner": "ai"}`, `setScores=[{player:0, ai:6}]`, stats — `result_payload()` carries
  that same line and the sim's own win flag, `finish_route(true)` reports
  `payload_ready` and parks the payload in `Config.pending_result`;
- a host booted with that payload mounts `result`, whose `score_numbers()` equals the
  payload's, and whose `rematch_route()` is `Match.tscn`;
- the pause seam: explicit true/false, idempotent echo, ESC hierarchy, and a rematch
  that leaves the match running; `leave_match()` exposed;
- the OSK panel is bound to the input lane's model and carries the reference's rows;
- `ui_legacy = true` builds the ported column with no router (the diagnostic path).

## 3. Engine failures found while running the flow, and repaired

| failure (engine line) | file | repair |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `Parse Error: There is already a variable named "stack"` — the screen could not load at all | `CharactersScreen.gd` | the duplicate `var stack` dropped; the outer one is the same node |
| `Cannot call method 'add_child' on a null value` on the tutorial row | `ControlLegend.gd` | the row's root is a `Button` there, not a `Container`; the child is added through the Control and laid over it (`MOUSE_FILTER_IGNORE`) — the link rendered nowhere before, while the screen reported the button as present |
| `Invalid access to property or key 'cap_up'` on every tutorial build | `SmashTutorial.gd` | the bandeja row carries `cap_down` only — read through `get` |
| `Can't change orientation of HBoxContainer` on every build and resize | `SmashTutorial.gd` | a BoxContainer's orientation is fixed at construction; the two column rules swap the container for the other class and re-parent |
| `Invalid assignment of property or key 'position' ... on 'Nil'` on every start/rematch in harness/headless | `match_controller.gd::_sync_views` | the views only exist when the models were loaded — guard added |
| the audits themselves could not load (`non-static palette_keys()` called on the class, untyped `var :=`) | `pause_audit.gd`, `osk_touch_audit.gd`, `screen_profile_audit.gd` | instance calls (every non-replay screen's `palette_keys()` is an instance method; only `ReplayOverlay`'s is static) and explicit types |

