### The ported lane's own suite (run last, same guard)

`game_slice_test.gd` — **PASS 342/342, exit 0**, one engine-counted line:

```
ERROR: arena_library: unknown arena id 'nope' (have: officina, locomotive, clockwork,
cattedrale, forgia, tempesta, abissale, caldera, orrery)
```

That is the recorded, allow-listed line — the suite's own deliberate unknown-id probe
(`game_slice_test.gd:1903`, `Arena.build("nope", …) == null`), which the port's strict
log gate already allows (`godot/game/check_log.sh:15-23`, `ALLOW_ARENA`; the baseline
records it verbatim in `uir-00-baseline-gates.log:90-105`). Beside it the run prints the
known shutdown note as a `WARNING` (`2 ObjectDB instances were leaked at exit`), which is
the same engine shutdown report the baseline allow-lists (`ALLOW_SHUTDOWN`) and is not
counted as an error. No other engine line, and `SCRIPT ERROR` count 0.

### The two audits the last steer named, re-run clean (separate counts)

| audit | exit | `SCRIPT ERROR` | `Parse Error` | other `ERROR:` | checks |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| pause_audit | 0 | **0** | **0** | 0 | PASS 176/176 |
| osk_touch_audit | 1 | **0** | **0** | 0 | FAIL 171/177 (6 real check failures, §5) |

Root cause of the parse failures: the audits called `palette_keys()` statically on the
class, and every non-replay screen's `palette_keys()` is an instance method
(`PauseOverlay.gd:907`, `OskPanel.gd:209`, `TouchControls.gd:271`; only
`ReplayOverlay.gd:331` is `static`). Repaired in the audits by calling through the
instances the audits already hold, which is the repo's own convention; the replay audit's
static calls are correct and were left alone.

## 5. The reds, classified

None of the red audits below mount through the new host: each mounts its own scene (or
its own router) directly, and none of the screens involved were edited by this wave —
except `CharactersScreen.gd`, whose parse error (above) was fixed here, which is why
its remaining single check is new information rather than a regression. Their own
tickets' evidence logs carry different tallies (`screen_characters_audit … PASS 130/130`,
`FAIL 73/76` for help), i.e. these are lane drifts in the current dirty tree, not
consequences of the integration seams.

- `osk_touch_audit` (6): `osk/no_targets_while_closed` expects 0 while the panel's
  accessor returns the built grid (the host itself only registers targets while the
  model is open); one grid key is not a target (52 vs 51); a row-order geometry check;
  the closed signal carries no field id; two touch checks (default instance palette,
  a screen-touch press driving the action).
- `screen_characters_audit` (1): unlocked picker cards do not carry the same strip set
  (`["maestro"]` differs).
- `screen_help_audit` (2 checks + 3 engine): the audit calls `HelpScreen.title_control()`
  (missing) and finds no `Title` node; the cap swap shows the port's Godot letters
  where the reference's glyphs are expected; one narrow-frame overflow.
- `screen_history_audit` (5 + 6 engine): the three boxes read empty (`["","",""]`),
  `Main/Mode` node path drift, `Array[Dictionary]` assignment error.
- `screen_challenges_audit` (4 + 2 engine): arena rows do not carry the frozen ids,
  done-row border, `SectionTitle` path drift, `four columns at 1280` inverted in the audit.
- `screen_profile_audit` (18 + 4 engine): the stat boxes/labels read empty and two
  node lookups fail (`Stat0/Value`, objectives row, unlock button) — the screen's
  `_fill_stats` output is not reachable at audit time.
- `ui_legibility_audit` (94): contrast and containment on the screens that now get
  walked (`arena` player-mode buttons, `challenges` name/state labels, `help`
  controller tab, `profile` progress rows, `feedback` diagnostics) plus two containment
  failures on `feedback`. Backgrounds read as `#ffffff`/`#999999` where the theme has
  no value for the node, which is what the ratios report.
- `screen_menu_audit` / `screen_feedback_audit` pass with engine lines of their own
  (1 and 3 respectively); they are logged in `/tmp/padel-uir22/audit-*.log`.

